    <statement><p>Let <m>y = 8 x^{3} + \frac{6 x^{4}}{x^{-6}} - 7 x^{5} + 1</m>.</p>
<p>(a) What power function does the function above resemble?</p>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> (Enter the entire power function, not just the degree of the power function.)</p>
<p>(b) Describe the long-run behavior of the polynomial.  Enter <em>INFINITY</em> or <em>-INFINITY</em> to denote <m>\infty</m> or <m>- \infty</m>.</p>
<p><m>y</m> goes to <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/> as <m>x \to \infty</m>.</p>
<p><m>y</m> goes to <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0003"/> as <m>x \to - \infty</m>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6x^{10}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\infty </m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\infty </m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



Since the leading term of the polynomial is <m>6 x^{10}</m>, the value of <m>y</m> goes to <m>\infty</m> as <m>x \to \infty</m> and <m>\infty</m> as <m>x \to - \infty</m>.





</solution>
